+  'elig.uktour.land': 'If you need land, you must own it. Land in the name of a close relative also works, if it is pledged to the bank as the first security. Leased land is allowed if the lease is longer than the time you take to repay the loan, and you have not failed to repay any bank or lender.',
+
+  'sdata.uk_minority.description': 'Government money for unemployed people of minority communities in Uttarakhand who take a bank loan of Rs.1 lakh to Rs.10 lakh to start their own work. You get 25% of the loan, at least Rs.25,000 and at most Rs.2,50,000. The bank charges its usual interest on the loan.',
+  'sdata.uk_minority.support': '25% of the loan as government money, Rs.25,000 to Rs.2,50,000',
+  'elig.ukminority.community': 'You must be a permanent resident of Uttarakhand and belong to a minority community: Muslim, Sikh, Christian, Parsi, Buddhist or Jain.',
+  'elig.ukminority.age': 'You must be between 18 and 55 years old.',
+  'elig.ukminority.income': 'Your family\'s income from all sources for the year must not be more than Rs.2,50,000, or your family must be below the poverty line.',
+  'elig.ukminority.share': 'You get the government money only with a loan of Rs.1 lakh to Rs.10 lakh, and you put in 15% of the project cost yourself.',
+  'elig.ukminority.select': 'The department puts out a notice asking for applicants. You apply at the office of the District Minority Welfare Officer or the District Social Welfare Officer, and a selection committee interviews the applicants.',
+
+  'sdata.uk_bee.description': 'Helps farmers in Uttarakhand take up bee-keeping. Government money covers 40% of the cost of bee boxes and colonies, up to Rs.2,000 each. You can get 50 boxes in plain areas and 25 in hilly areas, and Rs.350 for each colony kept in your own orchard. Training is free for seven days, and each trainee is paid Rs.1,050 in all.',
+  'sdata.uk_bee.support': 'Government pays 40% of bee box and colony costs, with free training',
+  'elig.ukbee.farmer': 'You must be a farmer who wants to take up bee-keeping.',
+  'elig.ukbee.apply': 'You apply at the nearest Horticulture Mobile Team Centre. People are chosen in the order they apply, for as long as the budget lasts.',
+
+  'sdata.uk_cfpc.description': 'A community centre where people and farmers of Uttarakhand learn to process fruits and vegetables, add value to their produce and earn more. Training lasts 10 days in towns and 15 days in villages. You can also have your food processed at the centre.',
+  'sdata.uk_cfpc.support': 'Training and food processing at the centre for a small fee',
+  'elig.ukcfpc.fees': 'A fee of Rs.15 is charged for each trainee, and Rs.15 for each kilogram processed, for which you bring the raw material.',
+  'elig.ukcfpc.visit': 'You visit the nearest Community Food Processing Centre, and places are given in the order people come.',
+
+  'sdata.uk_hoh.description': 'A brand for the local products of Uttarakhand, run by the Rural Development Department. It works on branding, marketing, quality and packaging so that products of self-help groups, women entrepreneurs and community groups can reach bigger markets in India and abroad.',
+  'sdata.uk_hoh.support': 'Help with branding, packaging and selling local products',
+  'elig.ukhoh.member': 'You must be a member of a self-help group, community organisation, collective or cluster-level federation formed under a scheme of an Uttarakhand government department, or a woman entrepreneur.',
+
+  'sdata.uk_nulm.description': 'Bank loans of up to Rs.2 lakh for people in towns and cities of Uttarakhand to start or grow a small business, with part of the interest paid by the central and state governments. You get the form from your municipal body, which checks it and sends it to the bank.',
+  'sdata.uk_nulm.support': 'Bank loan up to Rs.2 lakh, with part of the interest paid',
+  'elig.uknulm.income': 'Your family\'s income for the year must be less than Rs.3 lakh.',
+
+  // --- added 31 Oct 2026, Gujarat state schemes ---
+  'sdata.gj_tribal_int.description': 'For Scheduled Tribe people in the tribal areas of Gujarat who take a bank loan to start work of their own. The government gives 6% interest help on a loan of up to Rs.5 lakh.',
+  'sdata.gj_tribal_int.support': '6% interest help on a bank loan of up to Rs.5 lakh',
+  'elig.gjtribal.st': 'You must be a Scheduled Tribe person.',
+  'elig.gjtribal.area': 'You must live in a tribal area of Gujarat.',
+  'elig.gjtribal.loan': 'You must have taken a bank loan to start work of your own.',
+  'elig.gjtribal.office': 'You apply at the office of the Project Administrator of the Gujarat Tribal Development Corporation in Gandhinagar, or at a tribal district office.',
+
+  'sdata.gj_jgvy.description': 'For artisans, small entrepreneurs and self-help groups who want to start a new village industry. The government pays 25% of the first Rs.10 lakh of the cost, or 30% for Scheduled Caste, Scheduled Tribe, women and people with a disability, and 10% of the cost above that, up to Rs.25 lakh.',
+  'sdata.gj_jgvy.support': 'Government pays 25% of the first Rs.10 lakh (30% for some groups)',
+  'elig.gjjgvy.who': 'You must be an individual artisan or entrepreneur, or a member of an active Grade-II self-help group that makes small-scale products. You must not be applying on behalf of a partnership firm, private company, joint venture, HUF or similar business.',
+  'elig.gjjgvy.age': 'You must be between 25 and 50 years old.',
+  'elig.gjjgvy.class10': 'You must have passed at least Class 10 at a recognised school board.',
+  'elig.gjjgvy.experience': 'You must have at least one year of experience in the work you plan to do, or training in it from a recognised institute.',
+  'elig.gjjgvy.village': 'Your project must be in a rural area where not more than 20,000 people live, with a 24-hour three-phase electricity supply.',
+  'elig.gjjgvy.cost': 'The cost of the project must be from Rs.1 lakh to Rs.25 lakh. It can include machinery, raw materials and money to run the business (up to 10% of the total), but not land or buildings. The government money comes only after your unit has run well for 2 years.',
+
+  'sdata.gj_dtaiss.description': 'For handloom and handicraft artisans registered in Gujarat. A bank loan of up to Rs.1 lakh for machinery, tools or raw materials. The government pays a share of the loan one time, and 7% interest help every six months for up to 3 years.',
+  'sdata.gj_dtaiss.support': 'Loan of up to Rs.1 lakh, and the government pays 20% to 25% of it',
+  'elig.gjdtaiss.skill': 'You must have skills in handloom or handicraft work.',
+  'elig.gjdtaiss.registered': 'You must be registered as an artisan with Indext-C of the Cottage and Rural Industries Department, and hold an identity card from the Development Commissioner (Handloom or Handicraft) or from Indext-C, or a temporary certificate from the General Manager of the District Industries Centre.',
+  'elig.gjdtaiss.margin': 'The government pays 20% of the loan if you are a man in the general category, and 25% if you are a Scheduled Caste, Scheduled Tribe or woman applicant, or are blind or have a disability of 40% or more. It is paid once, after the loan is given.',
+  'elig.gjdtaiss.repay': 'You repay the loan with interest in 12 to 36 monthly instalments, as the bank fixes. You must pay each instalment on time, must not have failed to repay a bank, and must use the loan only for the purpose it was given for.',
+
+  'sdata.gj_mahila.description': 'For Scheduled Caste women from low-income families in Gujarat who want to start a small business. A loan of Rs.50,000 at 6% interest a year. The state puts in 95% of it (Rs.47,500) and you put in 5% (Rs.2,500). The monthly instalment may be about Rs.1,445 for 36 months.',
+  'sdata.gj_mahila.support': 'Loan of Rs.50,000 at 6% interest, repaid over 36 months',
+  'elig.gjmahila.permanent': 'You must be a permanent resident of Gujarat.',
+  'elig.gjdaadc.sc': 'You must be a Scheduled Caste person.',
+  'elig.gjmahila.aay': 'You must be from an Antyodaya Anna Yojana (AAY) family, or from an economically backward class.',
+  'elig.gjdaadc.income': 'Your family\'s income for a year must not be more than Rs.3 lakh.',
+  'elig.gjmahila.plan': 'You must plan to start a small business or work of your own.',
+  'elig.gjdaadc.online': 'You apply online, on the website of the Dr. Ambedkar Antyodaya Development Corporation.',
+
+  'sdata.gj_smallbiz.description': 'For Scheduled Caste people from Antyodaya Anna Yojana families in Gujarat who want to start or grow a small business. A loan of up to Rs.1,25,000 at 4% interest a year, repaid over 60 months, with two guarantors. The state puts in the whole amount, so you put in no share. The monthly instalment is about Rs.2,302 at most.',
+  'sdata.gj_smallbiz.support': 'Loan up to Rs.1,25,000 at 4% interest, repaid over 60 months',
+  'elig.gjsmallbiz.aay': 'You must be from an Antyodaya Anna Yojana (AAY) family.',
+  'elig.gjsmallbiz.intent': 'You must plan to start or grow a small business or trade.',
+  'elig.gjsmallbiz.guarantors': 'You must have two guarantors, people who agree to stand behind your loan.',
+
+  'sdata.gj_selfemp.description': 'For unemployed Scheduled Tribe people in Gujarat. Loans of Rs.50,000 to Rs.5 lakh, depending on the business you choose, at 4% interest a year, to start any of 85 businesses the department has named.',
+  'sdata.gj_selfemp.support': 'Loan of Rs.50,000 to Rs.5 lakh at 4% interest',
+  'elig.gjselfemp.unemployed': 'You must have no job when you apply.',
+  'elig.gjselfemp.list': 'Your business must be one of the 85 businesses the department has named, and the loan amount depends on the business.',
+  'elig.gjselfemp.online': 'You apply online, on the website of the Gujarat Tribal Development Corporation.',
+
+  'sdata.gj_fvp.description': 'Hands-on training in preserving and canning fruits and vegetables, and in growing them in a kitchen garden. The training lasts 2 to 5 days. The government meets Rs.500 per person per day: Rs.250 is paid to you as a stipend and Rs.250 goes on training material, experts and other costs.',
+  'sdata.gj_fvp.support': 'Stipend of Rs.250 a day during a training of 2 to 5 days',
+  'elig.gjfvp.willing': 'You must be willing to take part in skills training on fruit and vegetable growing.',
+  'elig.gjfvp.online': 'You apply online, on the I-Khedut portal.',
+
+  'sdata.gj_micro.description': 'For small business owners of the Rabari and Bharwad communities in Gujarat. Loans of up to Rs.1,25,000 at 5% interest a year, covering 95% of the cost of the project.',
+  'sdata.gj_micro.support': 'Loan up to Rs.1,25,000 at 5% interest',
+  'elig.gjmicro.caste': 'You must be from the Rabari or Bharwad community, which is among the socially and educationally backward classes.',
+  'elig.gjmicro.age': 'You must be between 21 and 45 years old.',
+  'elig.gjmicro.income': 'Your income for a year must not be more than Rs.3 lakh.',
+  'elig.gjmicro.share': 'The loan covers 95% of the cost, and you put in the other 5%.',
+  'elig.gjmicro.online': 'You apply online, on the DAAD Online portal.',
+
+  'sdata.gj_vahan.description': 'For self-employed people in Gujarat in the unreserved category. A loan for the on-road cost of a vehicle such as a rickshaw, loading rickshaw, Maruti car or jeep taxi, at 5% simple interest a year, or 4% for women.',
+  'sdata.gj_vahan.support': 'Loan for a vehicle\'s on-road cost, at 5% interest (4% for women)',
+  'elig.gjvahan.unreserved': 'You must belong to the unreserved category, not a reserved one.',
+  'elig.gjvahan.age': 'You must be between 18 and 50 years old.',
+  'elig.gjvahan.licence': 'You must have a valid driving licence.',
+  'elig.gjvahan.income': 'Your family\'s income for a year must not be more than Rs.6 lakh.',
+  'elig.gjvahan.vehicle': 'The vehicle you buy must be pledged to the corporation as security for the loan, and you repay the loan in equal monthly instalments over 5 years.',
+  'elig.gjvahan.limits': 'Only one person from a family can get this, and at most 5 people are chosen in a village.',
+
+  // --- added 31 Oct 2026, Madhya Pradesh state schemes ---
+  'sdata.mp_msy.description': 'For people in Madhya Pradesh who start their own work with a bank loan of Rs.50,000 to Rs.10 lakh. The government pays 15% of the project cost, up to Rs.1 lakh (30%, up to Rs.2 lakh, for some groups). It also helps with interest: 5% a year of the project cost (6% for women), up to Rs.25,000 a year, for up to 7 years.',
+  'sdata.mp_msy.support': 'Government pays 15% to 30% of the cost, plus 5% a year interest help',
+  'elig.mpmsy.permanent': 'You must be a permanent resident of Madhya Pradesh.',
+  'elig.mpmsy.class5': 'You must have passed at least Class 5.',
+  'elig.mpmsy.taxpayer': 'Your family must not pay income tax.',
+  'elig.mpmsy.defaulter': 'You must not have failed to repay a loan to any bank.',
+  'elig.mpmsy.noOther': 'You must not be getting help from any other self-employment scheme.',
+  'elig.mpmsy.once': 'You can take the benefit of this scheme only once.',
+  'elig.mpmsy.margin': 'The higher share of 30%, up to Rs.2 lakh, is for families below the poverty line, Scheduled Castes, Scheduled Tribes, Other Backward Classes (not the better-off families among them), women, minorities and disabled people.',
+
+  'sdata.mp_myuy.description': 'For people in Madhya Pradesh who set up their own industry with a bank loan of Rs.10 lakh to Rs.2 crore. The government pays 15% of the capital cost, up to Rs.12 lakh (20%, up to Rs.18 lakh, for families below the poverty line). It also helps with interest: 5% a year of the capital cost (6% for women) for up to 7 years.',
+  'sdata.mp_myuy.support': 'Government pays 15% to 20% of the cost, plus 5% a year interest help',
+  'elig.mpmyuy.age': 'You must be between 18 and 40 years old.',
+  'elig.mpmyuy.class10': 'You must have passed at least Class 10.',
+
+  'sdata.mp_drivers.description': 'For registered drivers and conductors in Madhya Pradesh who buy their own vehicle on a bank loan, for a project costing Rs.20,000 to Rs.10 lakh. The government pays 15% of the project cost, up to Rs.1 lakh (30%, up to Rs.2 lakh, for some groups). It also helps with interest: 5% a year, up to Rs.25,000 a year, for up to 7 years.',
+  'sdata.mp_drivers.support': 'Government pays 15% to 30% of the cost, plus 5% a year interest help',
+  'elig.mpdrivers.registered': 'You must be a registered driver or conductor of a transport vehicle.',
+  'elig.mpdrivers.licence': 'You must have a valid commercial driving licence or conductor licence issued in Madhya Pradesh.',
+  'elig.mpdrivers.samagra': 'You must be registered on the Samagra Portal.',
+  'elig.mpdrivers.defaulter': 'You must not have failed to repay a loan to any nationalised bank, cooperative bank or other financial institution.',
+  'elig.mpdrivers.margin': 'The higher share of 30%, up to Rs.2 lakh, is for families below the poverty line, women, minorities and disabled people.',
+  'elig.mpdrivers.office': 'You apply at the District or Regional Transport Office.',
+
+  'sdata.mp_pathvendor.description': 'For poor small traders and street vendors in villages of Madhya Pradesh. A loan of up to Rs.10,000 through a bank, for low-cost equipment or money to run the business. If you are starting a new business, you first take training at a rural self-employment training institute, and after it the loan has no interest.',
+  'sdata.mp_pathvendor.support': 'Loan of up to Rs.10,000, with no interest after training',
+  'elig.mppath.rural': 'You must live in a rural area.',
+  'elig.mppath.trader': 'You must be a small trader or street vendor from a poor rural family.',
+  'elig.mppath.nodefault': 'You must not have failed to repay any earlier government loan.',
+  'elig.mppath.training': 'If you are starting a new business, you must first take training at a rural self-employment training institute (RSETI).',
+  'elig.mppath.online': 'You apply online on the Street Vendor Portal.',
+
+  'sdata.mp_goat.description': 'For landless workers, small farmers and marginal farmers in Madhya Pradesh who have goat farming experience. A government grant and a bank loan help you buy a goat unit (10+1) for milk and meat. The grant is 40% of the unit cost (60% for Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes), on a total unit cost of Rs.77,456.',
+  'sdata.mp_goat.support': '40% grant on a Rs.77,456 goat unit (60% for SC and ST)',
+  'elig.mpgoat.who': 'You must be a landless worker, a marginal farmer or a small farmer.',
+  'elig.mpgoat.experience': 'You must have earlier experience in goat farming.',
+  'elig.mpgoat.apply': 'You apply at the nearest veterinary institution of the Animal Husbandry Department. The grant is paid to the bank after the bank approves your loan.',
+
+  'sdata.mp_dairyplus.description': 'For livestock farmers in Sehore, Vidisha and Raisen districts of Madhya Pradesh, the only places where it runs for now. You get two pregnant Murrah buffaloes of good breed, each giving about 8 to 10 litres of milk a day. The government pays 50% of the cost (75% for Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes) and you pay the rest.',
+  'sdata.mp_dairyplus.support': 'Government pays 50% of the cost of two buffaloes (75% for SC and ST)',
+  'elig.mpdairy.district': 'You must live in Sehore, Vidisha or Raisen district, the only places where the scheme runs for now.',
+  'elig.mpdairy.farmer': 'You must be a livestock farmer.',
+  'elig.mpdairy.shed': 'You must have a shed and water for keeping two dairy animals.',
+  'elig.mpdairy.apply': 'You apply at the nearest veterinary office in your district, and the Gram Sabha, the Janpad Panchayat and the District Panchayat Agricultural Standing Committee approve it in turn.',
+
+  'sdata.mp_aitrain.description': 'For unemployed young people in Madhya Pradesh who want to work in dairy farming, and for chosen Gausevaks. You get 3 months of free training in artificial insemination (1 month of theory, 2 months of practical work) at a government-recognised institute. After training, a Gausevak gets Rs.4,000 and equipment worth Rs.18,000.',
+  'sdata.mp_aitrain.support': 'Free 3-month training, Rs.4,000 and equipment worth Rs.18,000',
+  'elig.mpai.unemployed': 'You must be an unemployed young person.',
+  'elig.mpai.interest': 'You should have a strong interest in dairy farming and artificial insemination.',
+  'elig.mpai.select': 'One person from each Gram Panchayat is chosen for the first training, with the approval of the Janpad Panchayat.',
+
+  // --- added 31 Oct 2026, Bihar state schemes ---
+  'sdata.br_startup.description': 'For young people in Bihar who run a new business registered in the state as a company or partnership. A seed loan of Rs.10 lakh with no interest for 10 years, and a Rs.3 lakh grant if your business joins training on its product and on finance. Shared office space is also on offer.',
+  'sdata.br_startup.support': 'Rs.10 lakh seed loan, no interest for 10 years, plus a Rs.3 lakh grant',
+  'elig.brstartup.entity': 'Your business must be a private limited company, a registered partnership firm or an LLP, and no more than 10 years can have passed since it was registered.',
+  'elig.brstartup.turnover': 'Your yearly turnover must not have been more than Rs.100 crore in any year since you registered.',
+  'elig.brstartup.innovation': 'Your business must offer new or better products or services, or have a plan that can grow and create many jobs or much wealth.',
+  'elig.brstartup.newbiz': 'A business made by splitting up or rebuilding an older business does not count as a start-up.',
+  'elig.brstartup.bihar': 'Your business must be registered in Bihar, have an office in Bihar, and pay its taxes in Bihar.',
+
+  'sdata.br_chai.description': 'For tea farmers in Kishanganj, Araria, Supaul, Purnia and Katihar districts of Bihar. You buy the plants yourself and the government pays towards them in two parts: 75% in the first year and the other 25% in the second if ninety per cent of the plants survive. It also pays 50% of the cost of tea machines, up to a limit.',
+  'sdata.br_chai.support': 'Government money for tea plants (75%, then 25%) and 50% on machines',
+  'elig.brchai.district': 'You must be from one of these districts of Bihar: Kishanganj, Araria, Supaul, Purnia or Katihar.',
+  'elig.brchai.farmer': 'You must be a farmer.',
+  'elig.brchai.land': 'You must have at least 2 acres of land, and more for some machines: 10 acres for a vehicle to carry tea leaves and 5 acres for a tea leaf collection shed.',
+  'elig.brchai.dbt': 'You must be registered as a farmer on the DBT portal with your Aadhaar number. You can apply online 48 hours after registering.',
+  'elig.brchai.machines': 'The government pays 50% of the cost of a machine, up to Rs.60,000 for a pruning machine, Rs.50,000 for a mechanical harvester, Rs.1,100 for plucking shears (at most 20), Rs.7,50,000 for a vehicle to carry tea leaves and Rs.37,500 for a tea leaf collection shed.',
+  'elig.brchai.exclusion': 'If you get money for planting a new tea area under this scheme, you cannot also get money for machines.',
+  'elig.brchai.select': 'People are chosen in the order they apply, and 30% of the places are kept for women.',
+
+  'sdata.br_mmuy_scst.description': 'For Scheduled Caste and Scheduled Tribe people in Bihar who want to start a business. You can get up to Rs.10 lakh: half (up to Rs.5 lakh) is a grant you do not pay back, and half (up to Rs.5 lakh) is a loan with no interest, or 1% interest in some parts of the scheme. Training is compulsory.',
+  'sdata.br_mmuy_scst.support': 'Up to Rs.10 lakh: half is a grant, half is a loan with no interest',
+  'elig.brmmuy.permanent': 'You must be a permanent resident of Bihar.',
+  'elig.brmmuy.scst': 'You must belong to a Scheduled Caste or Scheduled Tribe.',
+  'elig.brmmuy.education': 'You must have passed at least 10+2, Intermediate, ITI, a polytechnic diploma or an equivalent examination.',
+  'elig.brmmuy.age': 'You must be between 18 and 50 years old.',
+  'elig.brmmuy.firm': 'Your business must be owned by one person, or be a partnership firm.',
+  'elig.brmmuy.online': 'You apply online: register on the scheme\'s website with your Aadhaar number and a password, then fill in the form and upload your documents.',
+
+  'sdata.br_mmuy_ebc.description': 'For people of the Extremely Backward Classes in Bihar who want to start a business. You can get up to Rs.10 lakh: half (up to Rs.5 lakh) is a grant you do not pay back, and half (up to Rs.5 lakh) is a loan with no interest, or 1% interest in some parts of the scheme. Training is compulsory.',
+  'sdata.br_mmuy_ebc.support': 'Up to Rs.10 lakh: half is a grant, half is a loan with no interest',
+  'elig.brmmuy.ebc': 'You must belong to the Extremely Backward Classes.',
+
+  'sdata.br_mmuy_minority.description': 'For people of the minority communities in Bihar who want to start a business. You can get up to Rs.10 lakh: half (up to Rs.5 lakh) is a grant you do not pay back, and half (up to Rs.5 lakh) is a loan with no interest, or 1% interest in some parts of the scheme. Training is compulsory.',
+  'sdata.br_mmuy_minority.support': 'Up to Rs.10 lakh: half is a grant, half is a loan with no interest',
+  'elig.brmmuy.minority': 'You must belong to a minority community.',
+
+  'sdata.br_mmuy_yuva.description': 'For men of the general category and the backward classes in Bihar who want to start a business. You can get up to Rs.10 lakh: half (up to Rs.5 lakh) is a grant you do not pay back, and half (up to Rs.5 lakh) is a loan with no interest, or 1% interest in some parts of the scheme. Training is compulsory.',
+  'sdata.br_mmuy_yuva.support': 'Up to Rs.10 lakh: half is a grant, half is a loan with no interest',
+  'elig.brmmuy.men': 'Only men from the general category and the backward classes can apply.',
+
+  'sdata.br_minority_loan.description': 'For young people of the minority communities in Bihar (Muslim, Sikh, Christian, Buddhist, Jain and Parsi) who want a loan for work that gives employment. A loan of up to Rs.5 lakh at 5% interest a year, repaid in 20 instalments, one every three months, over 5 years. A 0.5% processing fee is deducted before you get the money.',
+  'sdata.br_minority_loan.support': 'Loan of up to Rs.5 lakh at 5% interest a year, repaid over 5 years',
+  'elig.brminloan.community': 'You must belong to a minority community: Muslim, Sikh, Christian, Buddhist, Jain or Parsi.',
+  'elig.brminloan.govjob': 'You must not be a government or semi-government employee.',
+  'elig.brminloan.income': 'Your family\'s income for the year must be less than Rs.4,00,000.',
+  'elig.brminloan.guarantor': 'For a loan up to Rs.1,00,000 you can stand guarantor yourself. For more, you need a guarantor of a kind the scheme lists, such as a government, semi-government or bank employee with at least 5 years of service left.',
+  'elig.brminloan.use': 'You can use the loan only for work that gives employment or an income.',
+  'elig.brminloan.apply': 'You apply offline at the District Minority Welfare Office, after the Bihar State Minorities Financial Corporation advertises for applications in daily newspapers. Ask the office whether your form goes to the district where you live permanently or the district where your business will start.',
+
+  // --- added 31 Oct 2026, Haryana state schemes ---
+  'sdata.hr_green.description': 'For Scheduled Caste people in Haryana who want to start work that helps reduce the greenhouse effect, such as an e-rickshaw, solar energy gadgets or a polyhouse. You get a loan for a project of up to Rs.2 lakh. The state\'s Scheduled Castes corporation pays 50% of the cost, up to Rs.10,000, and gives 10% as margin money.',
